<title>SWEDEN: Industrivarden sells Elit Fonster.</title>
<headline>Industrivarden sells Elit Fonster.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish industrial group Industrivarden on Monday said it had sold its 50 percent stake of window manufacturer Elit Fonster AB to pre-fabricated house manufacturer Myresjo AB.</p>
<p>This gives Myresjo, which is a subsidiary of building company Skanska AB, full ownership of Elit Fonster.</p>
<p>In a statement about the sale, Industrivarden did not release any financial details.</p>
<p>Elit Fonster is Sweden's biggest window manufacturer with a turnover of about 500 million crowns in 1996 and 650 staff in two factories in Lenhovda and Vetlanda, Skanska said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
